claim.claim-text:
a first adapter-to-wagon component configured to removably mount to the wagon;
a second adapter-to-wagon component configured to removably mount to the wagon;
a structural cross member extending between the two adapter-to-wagon components to provide structural support to the wagon;
a first adapter-to-seat component configured to removably couple to the child seat for securing the child seat to the wagon;
a second adapter-to-seat component configured to removably couple to the child seat for securing the child seat to the wagon; and
wherein the first adapter-to-seat component and the second adapter-to-seat component are fixedly positioned relative to one another;
a first vertical extension member coupled to the first adapter-to-seat component and a second vertical extension member coupled to the second adapter-to-seat component for positioning the child higher than a displaceable connecting walls such that the displaceable connecting wall does not need to be displaced from its upright use position in order to mount the child seat to the wagon;
wherein the child seat is configured to be mounted to the adapter-to-seat components with no interference with any part of the wagon.

a first adapter-to-wagon component configured to removably mount to the wagon;
a second adapter-to-wagon component configured to removably mount to the wagon;
a structural cross member extending between the two adapter-to-wagon components to provide structural support to the wagon;
a first adapter-to-seat component configured to removably couple to the child seat for securing the child seat to the wagon;
a second adapter-to-seat component configured to removably couple to the child seat for securing the child seat to the wagon; and
wherein the first adapter-to-seat component and the second adapter-to-seat component are fixedly positioned relative to one another;
a first vertical extension member coupled to the first adapter-to-seat component and a second vertical extension member coupled to the second adapter-to-seat component for positioning the child higher than a displaceable connecting walls such that the displaceable connecting wall does not need to be displaced from its upright use position in order to mount the child seat to the wagon;
removably mounting the first adapter-to-wagon component to a first wall of the wagon;
and
removably mounting the second adapter-to-wagon component to a second wall of the wagon;
wherein the child seat mounts to the adapter-to-seat components with no interference with any part of the wagon.
